Spec: Project/Flows

Purpose:
  Define how THIS project normally moves work between engineering
  stages — the concrete, project-level instance of the chain engine.
  This is NOT the chain engine itself (see chains/chains.sdd, ENGINE
  layer) and NOT a domain's real flow (see project/<domain>/flows.sdd,
  not yet created — forward reference, no domain exists yet).

Owns:
  This project's default stage sequence
  Project-level flow rules

DoesNotOwn:
  Chain lifecycle rules and stage definitions   (see ../chains/chains.sdd)
  Domain-specific flow overrides                (see project/<domain>/flows.sdd, future)
  Feature-level chain type selection            (see ./project.sdd -> [PM4])

Stages:

  AN, AR, DB, BE, API, FE, MD, QA, DO, VR

Default:

  AN > AR > DB > BE > API > FE > MD > QA > DO > VR

Rules:

  [F1] This file defines this project's default flow, not the chain engine itself.
  [F2] Global chain lifecycle rules remain owned by chains/chains.sdd — this file MUST NOT redefine them.
  [F3] A domain flow (project/<domain>/flows.sdd) MAY override the default sequence above when justified by that domain's own dependencies.
  [F4] A feature flow MAY add or remove stages from the default sequence based on its own dependency analysis.
  [F5] VR MUST remain the final verification stage in any resolved flow, regardless of domain/feature overrides.
  [F6] Flow changes MUST be traceable — recorded via decisions/rules.sdd or standards/states.sdd, not silently changed.

FlowResolution:

  Global chain rules (chains/chains.sdd)
    > Project flow (this file)
    > Domain flow (project/<domain>/flows.sdd)
    > Feature-specific stage overrides
    > Final executable chain

Portability:

  This file's Default sequence is this project's own instance and is
  NOT expected to be reusable as-is across other projects — unlike
  chains/chains.sdd, which MUST remain project-agnostic.

Navigation:
  Chain engine:     @../chains/chains.sdd
  Project model:     @./project.sdd
  Domain flow:        @./<domain>/flows.sdd (future, no domain exists yet)

State: +

BusinessFlows:

  IntegrationExecution:
    purpose: End-to-end flow for executing an external integration call
    applies_to:
      - integration-module
    steps:
      - receive_event: Event/message arrives (WebSocket, message queue, HTTP webhook, or polling claim)
      - validate_payload: Validate required fields (target_service, event_type, payload)
      - check_conditions: Evaluate integration conditions (business rules)
      - execute_precheck: Validate identity against external API (optional, config-driven)
      - build_request: Map internal fields to external API format using field mapping + transforms
      - call_external_api: Execute HTTP request with auth, timeout, content-type handling
      - process_response: Map external response back to internal fields
      - log_result: Persist request/response/execution_time to audit log
      - notify_if_needed: Dispatch notification if integration triggers one
    error_handling:
      - retry_on_failure: Increment retry_count, schedule retry with backoff
      - dead_letter: After max retries, mark as failed and alert
      - partial_success: Batch operations may partially succeed
    variants:
      - proactive_forward: send data to external system without prior request
      - reactive_webhook: External system calls back with result
      - status_poll: Periodic check of application status

  NotificationDispatch:
    purpose: Send outbound notifications through configured channels
    applies_to:
      - notification-service
    steps:
      - resolve_template: Load template config from settings
      - render_content: Replace placeholders with actual data values
      - check_daily_limit: Verify integration has not exceeded daily send limit
      - send_via_provider: Execute send through configured provider
      - log_result: Record send status, provider response, execution time
    error_handling:
      - retry_on_failure: Queue for retry (async via message queue or direct retry)
      - daily_limit_skip: Log and skip, do not retry
      - provider_fallback: Try alternative provider if primary fails
    variants:
      - async_mail: Queued via message broker for background processing
      - sync_notify: Immediate send (webhook, bot API)
      - template_email: HTML template with dynamic field replacement

  ScheduledSync:
    purpose: Periodic synchronization of external configuration data
    applies_to:
      - scheduled-sync
    steps:
      - fetch_config_once: Single API call to retrieve full configuration
      - execute_handlers_sequentially: Run sync handlers one by one to avoid DB contention
      - log_results: Record sync statistics (counts, errors, duration)
    handlers:
      - sync_config: External configuration data
      - sync_metadata: Reference data
    variants:
      - full_sync: All handlers run on every cycle
      - incremental_sync: Only changed items updated

  WebSocketEventIngestion:
    purpose: Real-time event intake via WebSocket with database persistence
    applies_to:
      - event-processor
    steps:
      - connect: Establish WebSocket connection with auth
      - heartbeat: Send periodic ping, expect pong response
      - receive_message: Parse incoming JSON message
      - deduplicate: Check event ID against acknowledged set to prevent duplicates
      - persist_to_db: Store raw event via persistence layer
      - acknowledge: Send event ID back to provider to confirm receipt
      - auto_restart: Periodic reconnect to prevent stale connections
    error_handling:
      - reconnect_on_close: Exponential backoff up to max attempts
      - fallback_to_polling: If WebSocket fails, activate polling loop
      - db_triggers: Database triggers auto-process persisted events

  BatchPreCheck:
    purpose: Validate identity against multiple integrations in parallel
    applies_to:
      - integration-module
    steps:
      - receive_job: Batch validation job created with identity values
      - discover_integrations: Find all active integrations with pre-check configured
      - execute_checks: Run pre-check for each integration sequentially or in parallel
      - aggregate_results: Collect pass/fail counts per integration
      - update_job_status: Mark job as completed with statistics
    error_handling:
      - integration_failure: Individual integration failure does not block others
      - timeout_per_integration: Each pre-check has its own timeout
      - partial_results: Store whatever results were collected

State: +
